Yeah, it's like when I first started writing

1311
00:52:44.020 --> 00:52:46.600
these emails that ended up

1312
00:52:46.600 --> 00:52:48.297
culminating into this book,

1313
00:52:48.297 --> 00:52:50.160
"Knowing Where to Look," you know,

1314
00:52:50.160 --> 00:52:53.643
I had been receiving Seth Godin's emails forever.

1315
00:52:54.510 --> 00:52:55.810
And then there was another friend

1316
00:52:55.810 --> 00:52:58.080
who you probably know, Jeff Kober,

1317
00:52:58.080 --> 00:53:00.852
from the recovery community,

1318
00:53:00.852 --> 00:53:01.753
a meditation teacher.

1319
00:53:03.304 --> 00:53:06.050
And he'd started writing these daily emails.

1320
00:53:06.050 --> 00:53:08.280
And I was like, oh man,

1321
00:53:08.280 --> 00:53:13.000
the thought to write a daily email just kept percolating.

1322
00:53:13.000 --> 00:53:15.020
And then eventually I decided, okay,

1323
00:53:15.020 --> 00:53:16.690
well I need to take this thing seriously,

1324
00:53:16.690 --> 00:53:20.190
but I'm gonna run out of content after like three weeks.

1325
00:53:20.190 --> 00:53:23.387
There's only so many stories that exist in the world.

1326
00:53:23.387 --> 00:53:25.300
And I had already written my book,

1327
00:53:25.300 --> 00:53:26.480
so I'd already like thought about

1328
00:53:26.480 --> 00:53:29.000
a lot of stories for my first book, "The Inner Gym,"

1329
00:53:29.000 --> 00:53:32.253
which we talked about on this podcast many years ago.

1330
00:53:34.541 --> 00:53:35.760
And so, yeah, the fear was there

1331
00:53:35.760 --> 00:53:38.170
and the fear was just as intimidating

1332
00:53:38.170 --> 00:53:40.810
as the idea was inspiring.

1333
00:53:40.810 --> 00:53:44.060
And, but again, you know I just had to start

1334
00:53:44.060 --> 00:53:45.820
and sure enough after two or three weeks,

1335
00:53:45.820 --> 00:53:47.180
I ran out of content,

1336
00:53:47.180 --> 00:53:48.980
but then something really interesting happened

1337
00:53:48.980 --> 00:53:52.010
that I would never have discovered had I not started,

1338
00:53:52.010 --> 00:53:54.840
which is from showing up every day,

1339
00:53:54.840 --> 00:53:57.170
and Steven Pressfield talks about this,

1340
00:53:57.170 --> 00:53:59.170
this sort of muse-like

1341
00:54:01.780 --> 00:54:05.230
creativity started to kind of come through me.

1342
00:54:05.230 --> 00:54:06.950
And I was like, wow.

1343
00:54:06.950 --> 00:54:08.640
I literally would be

1344
00:54:08.640 --> 00:54:11.240
having to hit the send button in 10 minutes.

1345
00:54:11.240 --> 00:54:13.370
And I had been sitting there for two hours

1346
00:54:13.370 --> 00:54:16.720
trying to think of something interesting to say.

1347
00:54:16.720 --> 00:54:19.433
And then in the final five minutes

1348
00:54:19.433 --> 00:54:21.260
it would like come through me,

1349
00:54:21.260 --> 00:54:23.080
and I would write it down and you get this feeling,

1350
00:54:23.080 --> 00:54:24.253
okay, this is it.

1351
00:54:25.240 --> 00:54:26.520
And then you would send it out.

1352
00:54:26.520 --> 00:54:28.280
And the next day, same thing would happen.

1353
00:54:28.280 --> 00:54:29.500
Maybe you have a little more time,

1354
00:54:29.500 --> 00:54:31.370
but I just realized that

1355
00:54:32.370 --> 00:54:34.150
if you keep showing up

1356
00:54:34.150 --> 00:54:37.930
you don't have to figure out what to do,

1357
00:54:37.930 --> 00:54:40.240
you just have to make the space for it.

1358
00:54:40.240 --> 00:54:41.903
It's kind of like that story I told about,

1359
00:54:41.903 --> 00:54:43.623
I don't know if you remember the Moses story,

1360
00:54:46.815 --> 00:54:49.180
but it's one of my favorite stories in the book,

1361
00:54:49.180 --> 00:54:51.360
where it's a biblical story,

1362
00:54:51.360 --> 00:54:53.340
where, you know we think about Moses

1363
00:54:53.340 --> 00:54:57.130
as this kind of charismatic leader of the Hebrews,

1364
00:54:57.130 --> 00:54:58.790
and, you know, he went and faced Pharaoh

1365
00:54:58.790 --> 00:55:00.500
and all of these things.

1366
00:55:00.500 --> 00:55:02.680
But the reality of that story,

1367
00:55:02.680 --> 00:55:03.950
according to historians,

1368
00:55:03.950 --> 00:55:07.590
was that Moses was a reluctant leader, right?

1369
00:55:07.590 --> 00:55:08.890
When he was at the Burning Bush

1370
00:55:08.890 --> 00:55:11.784
and got the message from God to go to Pharaoh

1371
00:55:11.784 --> 00:55:13.540
to demand they let his people go.

1372
00:55:13.540 --> 00:55:14.550
So Moses hesitated.

1373
00:55:14.550 --> 00:55:16.360
He was like, he didn't want to do it,

1374
00:55:16.360 --> 00:55:19.780
because as they have now identified it,

1375
00:55:19.780 --> 00:55:21.780
Moses had a speech impediment.

1376
00:55:21.780 --> 00:55:22.903
So he was a stutterer.

1377
00:55:23.740 --> 00:55:26.110
So this stutterer who had never been

1378
00:55:26.110 --> 00:55:27.670
in a leadership position in his life

1379
00:55:27.670 --> 00:55:31.350
is being told from God

1380
00:55:31.350 --> 00:55:34.130
to go to the most powerful, most dangerous person

1381
00:55:34.130 --> 00:55:35.780
in the entire land,

1382
00:55:35.780 --> 00:55:38.050
and make a demand on this property.

1383
00:55:38.050 --> 00:55:39.650
Tell him to give his property away.

1384
00:55:39.650 --> 00:55:40.900
So you can imagine,

1385
00:55:40.900 --> 00:55:43.800
his first reaction is, you got the wrong person.

1386
00:55:43.800 --> 00:55:44.700
You know, and God's like,

1387
00:55:44.700 --> 00:55:47.696
no you're the perfect person for this,

1388
00:55:47.696 --> 00:55:49.417
because you have to rise to the occasion.

1389
00:55:49.417 --> 00:55:52.380
And so then Moses asks the most sensible question

1390
00:55:52.380 --> 00:55:54.490
that anybody would ask in a situation like that,

1391
00:55:54.490 --> 00:55:57.050
which is, let's suppose I were able

1392
00:55:57.050 --> 00:56:00.430
to get in front of Pharaoh, if that's even possible,

1393
00:56:00.430 --> 00:56:01.400
which it's probably not,

1394
00:56:01.400 --> 00:56:04.343
but let's just run this hypothetical out a little further.

1395
00:56:05.400 --> 00:56:06.393
What would I say?

1396
00:56:07.380 --> 00:56:10.270
And God said, don't worry about that.

1397
00:56:10.270 --> 00:56:13.220
Just get in front of him, and then you'll know what to say.

1398
00:56:14.070 --> 00:56:16.553
And that's kind of it, you know, that's the path.

1399
00:56:16.553 --> 00:56:18.007
like you want the whole blueprint,

1400
00:56:18.007 --> 00:56:20.893
and it's like, no, no, no, no, just take the first step.

1401
00:56:21.890 --> 00:56:23.380
And that's exactly what happened to me.

1402
00:56:23.380 --> 00:56:25.240
I started writing these things.

1403
00:56:25.240 --> 00:56:27.510
I didn't, I knew I was gonna run out of content.

1404
00:56:27.510 --> 00:56:29.100
I didn't know what I was gonna say after that.

1405
00:56:29.100 --> 00:56:32.020
And, I would just had that message inside.

1406
00:56:32.020 --> 00:56:34.040
Just write what you know now,

1407
00:56:34.040 --> 00:56:36.040
and then you'll figure out what to say next.

1408
00:56:36.040 --> 00:56:37.340
Right, yeah, you have this quote,

1409
00:56:37.340 --> 00:56:39.010
something about,

1410
00:56:39.010 --> 00:56:40.810
that's profound, something about how

1411
00:56:41.750 --> 00:56:43.040
the next steps aren't revealed

1412
00:56:43.040 --> 00:56:44.320
until you take the first step.

1413
00:56:44.320 --> 00:56:46.440
And I think we're all victims

1414
00:56:46.440 --> 00:56:50.788
to one degree or another of analysis paralysis.

1415
00:56:50.788 --> 00:56:53.410
We want to know what the map looks like in its entirety

1416
00:56:53.410 --> 00:56:54.890
before we even begin,

1417
00:56:54.890 --> 00:56:56.730
and so we never get out of the starting gate.

1418
00:56:56.730 --> 00:56:58.290
And I know this,

1419
00:56:58.290 --> 00:57:00.440
all the things that I've created

1420
00:57:00.440 --> 00:57:01.760
started with taking a step

1421
00:57:01.760 --> 00:57:03.310
and having no idea where it would head,

1422
00:57:03.310 --> 00:57:06.340
but having on some level some trust

1423
00:57:06.340 --> 00:57:08.040
that if I take that step,

1424
00:57:08.040 --> 00:57:10.420
that that next step will present itself,

1425
00:57:10.420 --> 00:57:12.370
and it's never failed me.

1426
00:57:12.370 --> 00:57:13.713
And I think also,

1427
00:57:14.880 --> 00:57:17.610
the lesson in what you just shared

1428
00:57:17.610 --> 00:57:22.610
is this idea that it's a witch's brew

1429
00:57:23.360 --> 00:57:27.750
or this recipe between practicality and mysticism.

1430
00:57:27.750 --> 00:57:31.190
Like the practical aspect of showing up every single day,

1431
00:57:31.190 --> 00:57:36.010
provides the space for the mystical unknown to enter,

1432
00:57:36.010 --> 00:57:38.860
and that's something Pressfield talks about all the time.

1433
00:57:40.270 --> 00:57:43.410
There's also shades of 12 step recovery.

1434
00:57:43.410 --> 00:57:45.250
Like when you get sober,

1435
00:57:45.250 --> 00:57:47.350
the prospect of never drinking again

1436
00:57:47.350 --> 00:57:48.780
is completely overwhelming.

1437
00:57:48.780 --> 00:57:50.900
And you're continually told time and time again,

1438
00:57:50.900 --> 00:57:51.920
you don't have to worry about that.

1439
00:57:51.920 --> 00:57:54.760
You just have to hit the pillow tonight sober.

1440
00:57:54.760 --> 00:57:55.820
You show up for the page.

1441
00:57:55.820 --> 00:57:58.120
What's my daily email going to be today?

1442
00:57:58.120 --> 00:58:00.140
I don't have to worry about the fact

1443
00:58:00.140 --> 00:58:01.780
that I've committed to doing it every day.

1444
00:58:01.780 --> 00:58:04.860
I just have to get this one thing done for the day

1445
00:58:04.860 --> 00:58:08.540
and trust that tomorrow when I open up to the page

1446
00:58:08.540 --> 00:58:11.460
that something will inspire me.

1447
00:58:11.460 --> 00:58:13.856
Yeah, it's a momentum game 100%.

1448
00:58:13.856 --> 00:58:15.070
And that's how this podcast started.

1449
00:58:15.070 --> 00:58:18.307
You know, when we talked about it before on my podcast.

1450
00:58:18.307 --> 00:58:19.700
You went to that warehouse in Hawaii

1451
00:58:19.700 --> 00:58:21.600
and just kind of let it rip.

1452
00:58:21.600 --> 00:58:22.433
There was no, I was like,

1453
00:58:22.433 --> 00:58:23.460
am I going to do a second one?

1454
00:58:23.460 --> 00:58:24.876
I don't know.

1455
00:58:24.876 --> 00:58:25.709
Like, this was fun.

1456
00:58:25.709 --> 00:58:26.542
Let's see where it goes.

1457
00:58:26.542 --> 00:58:28.370
But you learned about the sound,

1458
00:58:28.370 --> 00:58:30.500
you wouldn't know what to even think about the sound

1459
00:58:30.500 --> 00:58:33.270
until you actually have echo-y sound in the first.

1460
00:58:33.270 --> 00:58:34.420
Yeah, like I didn't know

1461
00:58:34.420 --> 00:58:37.041
that I probably shouldn't record this in a warehouse.

1462
00:58:37.041 --> 00:58:39.970
(laughing)

1463
00:58:39.970 --> 00:58:44.440
Or how am I gonna put these quote, you know,

1464
00:58:44.440 --> 00:58:47.180
these little monologues on Instagram with captions

1465
00:58:47.180 --> 00:58:48.920
that look all fancy like these other people do.

1466
00:58:48.920 --> 00:58:50.162
Well, I don't know.

1467
00:58:50.162 --> 00:58:51.200
I guess I have to just film something first

1468
00:58:51.200 --> 00:58:53.620
and there's this thing called the internet,

1469
00:58:53.620 --> 00:58:56.640
and there's seems to be a lot of answers on that.

1470
00:58:56.640 --> 00:59:01.380
Yeah, it's not like, you know, the answers may come,

1471
00:59:01.380 --> 00:59:02.390
if you don't do the work.

1472
00:59:02.390 --> 00:59:04.460
You actually have to do the work.

1473
00:59:04.460 --> 00:59:06.030
That's the requirement.

1474
00:59:06.030 --> 00:59:07.690
Yeah, you say, I love your quote.

1475
00:59:07.690 --> 00:59:10.230
Like "the work is the shortcut."

1476
00:59:10.230 --> 00:59:11.840
You know?

1477
00:59:11.840 --> 00:59:14.200
We're all looking for a way to avoid that,

1478
00:59:14.200 --> 00:59:16.560
but the work is the means

1479
00:59:16.560 --> 00:59:19.760
by which you find the answers to which you seek.

1480
00:59:19.760 --> 00:59:23.279
Just committing to taking those first steps

1481
00:59:23.279 --> 00:59:24.579
that's the shortest route.

1482
00:59:27.917 --> 00:59:29.060
We'll back in a sec, but first,

1483
