1508
01:00:23.660 --> 01:00:25.533
All right, let's get back into it.

1509
01:00:28.220 --> 01:00:31.400
There is a sort of precarious aspect

1510
01:00:31.400 --> 01:00:35.880
of stepping into this world of self-help,

1511
01:00:35.880 --> 01:00:40.510
and grappling with the ideas of curiosity and inspiration

1512
01:00:40.510 --> 01:00:44.500
and motivation and discipline and purpose and passion

1513
01:00:44.500 --> 01:00:46.840
and living your life in accordance with your values

1514
01:00:46.840 --> 01:00:48.150
and self-actualization.

1515
01:00:48.150 --> 01:00:49.790
Like these have all become

1516
01:00:49.790 --> 01:00:51.780
commodified to one degree or another,

1517
01:00:51.780 --> 01:00:55.723
and also sort of diluted in what they actually mean.

1518
01:00:56.590 --> 01:00:59.520
I think the interplay between these types

1519
01:00:59.520 --> 01:01:01.640
of words, you know, these words in general

1520
01:01:01.640 --> 01:01:04.883
are getting thrown around like fairly cavalierly,

1521
01:01:05.810 --> 01:01:09.410
reminds me that I'm not really even sure

1522
01:01:09.410 --> 01:01:10.913
we agree on what they,

1523
01:01:11.820 --> 01:01:14.010
they actually mean, how they operate,

1524
01:01:14.010 --> 01:01:15.720
how they interact with each other,

1525
01:01:15.720 --> 01:01:19.720
let alone how to properly understand and leverage them

1526
01:01:19.720 --> 01:01:24.280
to move your life in the direction of your aspirations.

1527
01:01:24.280 --> 01:01:27.890
These are all themes and words and topics

1528
01:01:27.890 --> 01:01:29.830
that you are grappling with in the book.

1529
01:01:29.830 --> 01:01:31.890
So I think it would be helpful and instructive

1530
01:01:31.890 --> 01:01:35.170
to spend a little bit of time talking about that.

1531
01:01:35.170 --> 01:01:38.250
I've got a story in the book about

1532
01:01:38.250 --> 01:01:40.500
how I was in a yoga class one day,

1533
01:01:40.500 --> 01:01:44.770
and the teacher popped up into a headstand

1534
01:01:44.770 --> 01:01:46.200
and he said, you know,

1535
01:01:46.200 --> 01:01:50.350
the headstand is the most spiritual pose in yoga.

1536
01:01:50.350 --> 01:01:52.153
And I was a yoga teacher.

1537
01:01:52.153 --> 01:01:52.986
Like fuck off.

1538
01:01:52.986 --> 01:01:54.140
And I was like, what the fuck is he talking about?

1539
01:01:54.140 --> 01:01:55.070
The headstand.

1540
01:01:55.070 --> 01:01:56.080
How do you qualify?

1541
01:01:56.080 --> 01:02:01.033
And then I realized that his definition of spiritual

1542
01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:05.020
was different from my definition of spiritual.

1543
01:02:05.020 --> 01:02:07.720
And that was a big aha for me,

1544
01:02:07.720 --> 01:02:09.390
because then I realized that every time

1545
01:02:09.390 --> 01:02:11.830
I get into these kind of confrontations with people,

1546
01:02:11.830 --> 01:02:14.130
and this is important also in the race conversation, right?

1547
01:02:14.130 --> 01:02:16.420
When we talk about racism,

1548
01:02:16.420 --> 01:02:19.680
or discrimination or whatever, systemic,

1549
01:02:19.680 --> 01:02:22.530
people have different definitions almost all the time.

1550
01:02:22.530 --> 01:02:25.350
Almost every relationship fight

1551
01:02:25.350 --> 01:02:26.790
is a result of people having

1552
01:02:26.790 --> 01:02:27.910
a different understanding

1553
01:02:27.910 --> 01:02:29.290
of what it means to feel safe,

1554
01:02:29.290 --> 01:02:31.580
or what it means to love someone, right?

1555
01:02:31.580 --> 01:02:33.970
Somebody may think love is always being there,

1556
01:02:33.970 --> 01:02:34.820
no matter what.

1557
01:02:34.820 --> 01:02:36.170
Someone else may think love

1558
01:02:38.073 --> 01:02:40.730
is allowing someone to fully express independently

1559
01:02:40.730 --> 01:02:41.870
and then coming together

1560
01:02:41.870 --> 01:02:44.210
and sharing whatever fulfillment they have inside.

1561
01:02:44.210 --> 01:02:46.060
Like there's different understandings

1562
01:02:46.060 --> 01:02:48.390
of all of these really simple terms

1563
01:02:48.390 --> 01:02:49.730
that we kind of take for granted.

1564
01:02:49.730 --> 01:02:53.100
And so, again, I'm not presenting myself

1565
01:02:53.100 --> 01:02:54.910
as the big guru with all the answers,

1566
01:02:54.910 --> 01:02:55.810
to all these questions.

1567
01:02:55.810 --> 01:02:57.140
What is self-actualization?

1568
01:02:57.140 --> 01:02:58.180
I'm just saying,

