01:45:09.320 --> 01:45:12.040
that level of honesty and authenticity

2607
01:45:12.040 --> 01:45:14.810
that only comes with somebody like Brandon

2608
01:45:14.810 --> 01:45:16.700
who can engender the level of trust,

2609
01:45:16.700 --> 01:45:20.510
where people feel comfortable sharing on that level.

2610
01:45:20.510 --> 01:45:22.080
And people know the difference between

2611
01:45:22.080 --> 01:45:26.810
artifice or some kind of performative version of that

2612
01:45:26.810 --> 01:45:28.340
and the very real thing.

2613
01:45:28.340 --> 01:45:29.173
And when you see,

2614
01:45:29.173 --> 01:45:31.520
these are just average people walking down the street,

2615
01:45:31.520 --> 01:45:32.796
they're not trying to, you know,

2616
01:45:32.796 --> 01:45:34.990
gain followers or anything like that.

2617
01:45:34.990 --> 01:45:37.830
They're just being honest about their experience

2618
01:45:37.830 --> 01:45:39.530
and there's a universality in that

2619
01:45:39.530 --> 01:45:40.610
that we can all connect to.

2620
01:45:40.610 --> 01:45:43.030
And that's what makes us feel closer to each other,

2621
01:45:43.030 --> 01:45:46.330
and is a recipe I think, you know, a curative recipe,

2622
01:45:46.330 --> 01:45:47.873
for so much of what ails us.

2623
01:45:47.873 --> 01:45:50.760
I think that's our true wealth, you know,

2624
01:45:50.760 --> 01:45:53.323
our life experience really is our true wealth.

2625
01:45:53.323 --> 01:45:57.290
If we can relate to it in a way

2626
01:45:57.290 --> 01:46:01.030
that kind of gets us out of our own head

2627
01:46:01.030 --> 01:46:02.470
or our own misery,

2628
01:46:02.470 --> 01:46:06.143
and allows us to be able to share it,

2629
01:46:07.190 --> 01:46:11.510
to help somebody else see things a little differently.

2630
01:46:11.510 --> 01:46:13.960
Because I'm sure anybody really could write this,

2631
01:46:15.040 --> 01:46:17.110
accumulate these stories just from their own life.

2632
01:46:17.110 --> 01:46:19.510
Most of the stories in here are my personal experiences,

2633
01:46:19.510 --> 01:46:20.343
and they're not,

2634
01:46:21.600 --> 01:46:23.870
I wouldn't consider them to be any more profound

2635
01:46:23.870 --> 01:46:25.060
than anyone else's experiences.

2636
01:46:25.060 --> 01:46:27.100
I was just paying attention a little differently

2637
01:46:27.100 --> 01:46:28.730
in the way that was unique to me

2638
01:46:28.730 --> 01:46:30.230
because of my life experience.

2639
01:46:30.230 --> 01:46:32.443
But someone else like Brandon or whoever,

2640
01:46:33.310 --> 01:46:35.130
has essentially done the same thing,

2641
01:46:35.130 --> 01:46:36.840
or helped other people do it.

2642
01:46:36.840 --> 01:46:40.163
And the way that they curate their story,

2643
01:46:41.580 --> 01:46:43.840
and again, Brandon talks about this.

2644
01:46:43.840 --> 01:46:45.350
It took practice.

2645
01:46:45.350 --> 01:46:48.420
He didn't just come off from the very first one.

2646
01:46:48.420 --> 01:46:49.550
For a very long time.

2647
01:46:49.550 --> 01:46:52.000
Yeah, he learned how to ask people questions

2648
01:46:52.000 --> 01:46:55.860
in a way that draws out the best parts of their story,

2649
01:46:55.860 --> 01:46:57.720
the most impactful parts of their story.

2650
01:46:57.720 --> 01:46:58.670
And that takes practice.

2651
01:46:58.670 --> 01:47:00.570
You learn from podcasting,

2652
01:47:00.570 --> 01:47:01.810
how to interview people in a way

2653
01:47:01.810 --> 01:47:04.620
that draws out the best parts of the story.

2654
01:47:04.620 --> 01:47:06.010
Brandon, you know, I mean,

2655
01:47:06.010 --> 01:47:08.240
it's another example,

2656
01:47:08.240 --> 01:47:10.870
certainly this isn't something that he white-boarded

2657
01:47:10.870 --> 01:47:13.980
and thought this is going to be a great career path for me.

2658
01:47:13.980 --> 01:47:15.950
He was following his curiosity.

2659
01:47:15.950 --> 01:47:17.210
He could have never predicted

2660
01:47:17.210 --> 01:47:18.760
that it would hit this cultural nerve,

2661
01:47:18.760 --> 01:47:21.270
and that people would be so interested in it.

2662
01:47:21.270 --> 01:47:24.010
And now it's like this huge thing.

2663
01:47:24.010 --> 01:47:26.480
And when I look at your career,

2664
01:47:26.480 --> 01:47:28.500
what you've written about in this book,

2665
01:47:28.500 --> 01:47:33.500
I see somebody who is in this sort of dance with the muse,

2666
01:47:35.750 --> 01:47:39.130
who's in communion with curiosity

2667
01:47:39.130 --> 01:47:41.610
and how that translates into actions

2668
01:47:41.610 --> 01:47:44.360
that you take or decisions that you make.

2669
01:47:44.360 --> 01:47:48.000
And it's a far cry from this

2670
01:47:48.000 --> 01:47:51.840
more mainstream paradigm of like, what is your goal?

2671
01:47:51.840 --> 01:47:52.960
Like, what's the vision?

2672
01:47:52.960 --> 01:47:54.460
Like, what are you working towards?

2673
01:47:54.460 --> 01:47:56.860
Like, you know, where is this all headed, Light?

2674
01:47:58.273 --> 01:47:59.700
I don't really operate like that.

2675
01:47:59.700 --> 01:48:02.140
And I do, I guest on podcasts,

2676
01:48:02.140 --> 01:48:03.260
I get asked that question,

2677
01:48:03.260 --> 01:48:06.060
like where do you see yourself in five years?

2678
01:48:06.060 --> 01:48:08.920
And I've caught myself like trying to answer

2679
01:48:08.920 --> 01:48:11.870
in the way that I see other people answering it.

2680
01:48:11.870 --> 01:48:13.360
And then I have to check myself

2681
01:48:13.360 --> 01:48:14.800
because it's like I don't,

2682
01:48:14.800 --> 01:48:16.550
I honestly don't think about that at all.

2683
01:48:16.550 --> 01:48:19.360
I'm literally just, what's the next cool thing

2684
01:48:19.360 --> 01:48:21.590
that I could do that gets me excited to get out of bed.

2685
01:48:21.590 --> 01:48:22.960
And I'm in a fortunate position,

2686
01:48:22.960 --> 01:48:24.150
where I have my needs met,

2687
01:48:24.150 --> 01:48:26.363
and I can entertain those kinds of ideas.

2688
01:48:27.200 --> 01:48:31.370
But I got to this point by doubling down on that,

2689
01:48:31.370 --> 01:48:34.363
as opposed to, you know, being very,

2690
01:48:36.250 --> 01:48:39.550
tactical or planning out these things.

2691
01:48:39.550 --> 01:48:42.290
This is how you're operating.

2692
01:48:42.290 --> 01:48:43.610
You never would have imagined-

2693
01:48:43.610 --> 01:48:47.040
No, and if I set this as a goal,

2694
01:48:47.040 --> 01:48:50.110
I would have missed the mark by a thousand miles

2695
01:48:50.110 --> 01:48:52.560
because I would've missed out on

2696
01:48:52.560 --> 01:48:55.120
why it got here, which was because, you know,

2697
01:48:55.120 --> 01:48:59.740
I just made the decision to do what interested me

2698
01:48:59.740 --> 01:49:02.663
as opposed to what seemed to make sense, I guess.

2699
01:49:04.473 --> 01:49:06.973
So I'm like throwing that back at you.

2700
01:49:08.060 --> 01:49:09.713
I mean, again,

2701
01:49:10.860 --> 01:49:13.160
I think the best thing I ever did in my life

2702
01:49:13.160 --> 01:49:15.110
was following the guidance

2703
01:49:15.110 --> 01:49:18.310
to quit my first real, quote unquote, real job,

2704
01:49:18.310 --> 01:49:19.970
when I was fresh out of college.

2705
01:49:19.970 --> 01:49:22.600
That was like the best thing I ever did,

2706
01:49:22.600 --> 01:49:25.140
because I realized that

2707
01:49:26.340 --> 01:49:28.380
what we've been taught by society

2708
01:49:28.380 --> 01:49:32.510
about what you need to do is not the real story,

2709
01:49:32.510 --> 01:49:34.550
'cause that's where my adventure,

2710
01:49:34.550 --> 01:49:37.830
that's how I opened the book is telling that story.

2711
01:49:37.830 --> 01:49:40.347
And the reason why I did it,

2712
01:49:40.347 --> 01:49:42.280
and I didn't have language for it at the time,

2713
01:49:42.280 --> 01:49:45.010
but I just kind of looked around

2714
01:49:45.010 --> 01:49:47.380
and it was a great job, it was a great agency.

2715
01:49:47.380 --> 01:49:49.130
Everyone was really wonderful, beautiful,

2716
01:49:49.130 --> 01:49:51.320
nice people, you know, no drama.

2717
01:49:51.320 --> 01:49:53.250
I looked forward to going there.

2718
01:49:53.250 --> 01:49:54.920
I would be the first there to arrive

2719
01:49:54.920 --> 01:49:56.513
and usually the last to leave.

2720
01:49:57.920 --> 01:49:59.890
But at the same time I looked at the people

2721
01:49:59.890 --> 01:50:03.300
who had achieved the most at that place.

2722
01:50:03.300 --> 01:50:05.350
And I didn't really feel like anybody was

2723
01:50:07.620 --> 01:50:10.980
fulfilled in the way that I ultimately

2724
01:50:10.980 --> 01:50:13.210
saw myself wanting to be fulfilled.

2725
01:50:13.210 --> 01:50:16.627
And so I said, okay, well this is where this goes, you know?

2726
01:50:16.627 --> 01:50:19.420
And that's a process that I've kind of applied

2727
01:50:19.420 --> 01:50:20.253
to other things.

2728
01:50:20.253 --> 01:50:24.670
If you are in a space with people

2729
01:50:24.670 --> 01:50:28.100
and you're thinking of investing your time into that,

2730
01:50:28.100 --> 01:50:31.100
whatever that space is about.

2731
01:50:31.100 --> 01:50:32.580
Look at the people who've been there the longest,

2732
01:50:32.580 --> 01:50:34.020
who've achieved the most,

2733
01:50:34.020 --> 01:50:37.670
and ask yourself are they where you want to be,

2734
01:50:37.670 --> 01:50:38.830
where you see yourself being?

2735
01:50:38.830 --> 01:50:41.270
And if so, then that's probably

2736
01:50:41.270 --> 01:50:42.980
where your path is leading you.

2737
01:50:42.980 --> 01:50:45.820
If not, then that's probably not your path.

2738
01:50:45.820 --> 01:50:48.650
And it doesn't really matter what the external rewards

2739
01:50:48.650 --> 01:50:50.640
of being in that space are.

2740
01:50:50.640 --> 01:50:53.440
It's really about what you feel about them inside.

2741
01:50:53.440 --> 01:50:55.600
And so we talked about this on the last podcast

2742
01:50:55.600 --> 01:50:57.460
is that when I, many years later,

2743
01:50:57.460 --> 01:51:02.360
when I came across my meditation teacher, Tom Knowles.

2744
01:51:02.360 --> 01:51:07.020
He embodied, for me, he embodied that state of fulfillment

2745
01:51:07.020 --> 01:51:08.810
that I had been looking for

2746
01:51:08.810 --> 01:51:10.700
without realizing that that's what I was looking for.

2747
01:51:10.700 --> 01:51:15.290
And immediately I knew that's the next milestone,

2748
01:51:15.290 --> 01:51:17.280
is to learn this thing,

2749
01:51:17.280 --> 01:51:19.510
to help other people in the way that I'm being helped,

2750
01:51:19.510 --> 01:51:21.290
because it always came, it came back to service.

2751
01:51:21.290 --> 01:51:25.560
That's how I kind of knew that that was really my path.

2752
01:51:25.560 --> 01:51:26.713
And there was no,

2753
01:51:29.764 --> 01:51:31.430
this is 2003,

2754
01:51:31.430 --> 01:51:35.190
so there's no teacher trainings or anything like that.

2755
01:51:35.190 --> 01:51:36.880
And I wrote about this in the book.

2756
01:51:36.880 --> 01:51:37.988
So I just had to trust

2757
01:51:37.988 --> 01:51:39.280
that it was gonna lead in that direction.

2758
01:51:39.280 --> 01:51:41.970
I just kept coming back and showing up and helping out.

2759
01:51:41.970 --> 01:51:44.700
And then eventually, many years later,

2760
01:51:44.700 --> 01:51:46.920
he invited me in some other of his proteges

2761
01:51:46.920 --> 01:51:49.450
to go to India and train as to become teachers.

2762
01:51:49.450 --> 01:51:51.130
And that really set me off

2763
01:51:51.130 --> 01:51:53.690
in a completely different direction from where I was before.

2764
01:51:53.690 --> 01:51:55.600
But there was this trust

2765
01:51:55.600 --> 01:51:57.963
that I had, that I had developed,

2766
01:52:00.700 --> 01:52:02.900
that developed, and I was very intentional about it.

2767
01:52:02.900 --> 01:52:06.060
I remember being 29 years old in my kitchen in Harlem

2768
01:52:06.060 --> 01:52:07.790
and saying to myself

2769
01:52:07.790 --> 01:52:10.010
I'm gonna follow my heart no matter what.

2770
01:52:10.010 --> 01:52:13.603
And after watching a Chris Rock movie.

2771
01:52:15.643 --> 01:52:16.476
It takes what it takes, man.

2772
01:52:16.476 --> 01:52:20.060
No, that story is where you talk about

2773
01:52:20.060 --> 01:52:22.210
this idea of wiggle room.

2774
01:52:22.210 --> 01:52:24.320
Like, even if you feel

2775
01:52:24.320 --> 01:52:26.990
like you're on a good path for yourself,

2776
01:52:26.990 --> 01:52:29.290
like not holding on too tightly to it,

2777
01:52:29.290 --> 01:52:32.670
and always making room to be malleable,

2778
01:52:32.670 --> 01:52:36.370
so that you can be available for

2779
01:52:36.370 --> 01:52:39.890
the magical opportunity of going to India,

2780
01:52:39.890 --> 01:52:41.240
in the case of your story.

2781
01:52:41.240 --> 01:52:42.600
And it's not about, you know,

2782
01:52:42.600 --> 01:52:44.730
'cause some people may look at or hear that and go,

2783
01:52:44.730 --> 01:52:46.350
that's just you not committing

2784
01:52:46.350 --> 01:52:49.078
to whatever you said you were gonna do.

2785
01:52:49.078 --> 01:52:52.793
And I would refine that and say what's really

2786
01:52:52.793 --> 01:52:56.670
your feeling about your path,

2787
01:52:56.670 --> 01:52:58.620
whatever that is, whether you have language for it or not,

2788
01:52:58.620 --> 01:53:00.910
is always gonna be there,

2789
01:53:00.910 --> 01:53:05.380
but the day-to-day plans may change,

2790
01:53:05.380 --> 01:53:06.805
about how you get there,

2791
01:53:06.805 --> 01:53:10.930
what occupation or what family lifestyle choices

2792
01:53:10.930 --> 01:53:12.257
you have to go through in order to get there.

2793
01:53:12.257 --> 01:53:14.410
And so that's where you want to be malleable

2794
01:53:14.410 --> 01:53:16.678
and be open to inspiration,

2795
01:53:16.678 --> 01:53:20.460
not in questioning the ultimate goal or plan.

2796
01:53:20.460 --> 01:53:22.180
You really can't go wrong

2797
01:53:22.180 --> 01:53:25.070
if you just keep following whatever.

2798
01:53:25.070 --> 01:53:28.530
Sure, but you also can't expect to be smiled upon

2799
01:53:28.530 --> 01:53:32.000
by you know, perhaps your peers and your colleagues.

2800
01:53:32.000 --> 01:53:32.833
No, that takes you

2801
01:53:32.833 --> 01:53:34.760
completely away from social proof.

2802
01:53:34.760 --> 01:53:36.330
You're gonna look like a dilettante.

2803
01:53:36.330 --> 01:53:37.163
You know what I mean?

2804
01:53:37.163 --> 01:53:39.330
Like, oh, this guy just goes from one thing to the next.

2805
01:53:39.330 --> 01:53:42.110
He can't really like stick with anything.

2806
01:53:42.110 --> 01:53:42.943
Did you read

2807
01:53:45.090 --> 01:53:46.720
David Epstein's book, "Range?"

2808
01:53:46.720 --> 01:53:47.553
No.

2809
01:53:47.553 --> 01:53:51.270
So it's a very interesting kind of study

2810
01:53:51.270 --> 01:53:55.930
of a variety of people who have excelled

2811
01:53:55.930 --> 01:53:57.140
in different fields,

2812
01:53:57.140 --> 01:54:00.220
from science and education to athletics

2813
01:54:00.220 --> 01:54:02.570
and art, et cetera.

2814
01:54:02.570 --> 01:54:05.040
And it belies this

2815
01:54:06.240 --> 01:54:09.530
sort of Malcolm Gladwell myth of the 10,000 hour rule,

2816
01:54:09.530 --> 01:54:12.280
and demonstrates that there are those people, of course,

2817
01:54:12.280 --> 01:54:13.950
the Tiger Woodses, and people like that,

2818
01:54:13.950 --> 01:54:15.960
but by and large,

2819
01:54:15.960 --> 01:54:18.010
most people who are fully expressed

2820
01:54:18.010 --> 01:54:19.840
and excelling at the highest level

2821
01:54:19.840 --> 01:54:22.890
of their specialized field

2822
01:54:22.890 --> 01:54:25.210
are people who earlier in life

2823
01:54:25.210 --> 01:54:26.580
did lots of different stuff,

2824
01:54:26.580 --> 01:54:27.740
and were the people

2825
01:54:27.740 --> 01:54:29.440
who just really couldn't commit to anything.

2826
01:54:29.440 --> 01:54:30.600
And as a result,

2827
01:54:30.600 --> 01:54:34.370
they develop this robustness of experience

2828
01:54:34.370 --> 01:54:37.330
that back to that idea of in retrospect, you know,

2829
01:54:37.330 --> 01:54:38.830
all the dots line up,

2830
01:54:38.830 --> 01:54:41.500
make perfect sense with where they end up,

2831
01:54:41.500 --> 01:54:43.870
but they are people of varied interests

2832
01:54:43.870 --> 01:54:45.830
and many different passions

2833
01:54:45.830 --> 01:54:49.880
who develop that capacity early to be malleable,

2834
01:54:49.880 --> 01:54:52.800
and flexible to have that wiggle room.

2835
01:54:52.800 --> 01:54:54.600
And, you know, it's those people

2836
01:54:54.600 --> 01:54:57.300
that we look at now as lazy dilettantes

2837
01:54:57.300 --> 01:55:00.750
who ultimately, it's reframing that and saying,

2838
01:55:00.750 --> 01:55:02.230
well, and you talk about this,

2839
01:55:02.230 --> 01:55:04.130
like how do you suspend judgment in the book?

2840
01:55:04.130 --> 01:55:06.240
Like maybe they're like,

2841
01:55:06.240 --> 01:55:07.920
we should look at this a little bit differently.

2842
01:55:07.920 --> 01:55:10.080
Perhaps they're in their exploratory phase

2843
01:55:10.080 --> 01:55:11.590
and they're gonna be magnificent

2844
01:55:11.590 --> 01:55:13.290
and amazing and world changing,

2845
01:55:13.290 --> 01:55:16.670
in something that they finally latch onto later in life.

2846
01:55:16.670 --> 01:55:19.110
Yeah, there is a story in there about how

2847
01:55:19.990 --> 01:55:21.970
I talk about leaving that first job

2848
01:55:21.970 --> 01:55:23.523
for the reasons that I left,

2849
01:55:25.279 --> 01:55:26.510
and then while I was writing,

2850
01:55:26.510 --> 01:55:29.020
I remember the day I wrote that story, I was in an Airbnb.

2851
01:55:29.020 --> 01:55:30.970
I think it was in London,

2852
01:55:30.970 --> 01:55:32.580
living out of a backpack.

2853
01:55:32.580 --> 01:55:33.930
Didn't own anything,

2854
01:55:33.930 --> 01:55:35.230
still don't own anything.

2855
01:55:35.230 --> 01:55:36.410
I've got a little money saved up,

2856
01:55:36.410 --> 01:55:38.180
but I had less saved up at the time.

2857
01:55:38.180 --> 01:55:39.520
And I was like, eh, you know,

2858
01:55:39.520 --> 01:55:42.420
compared to my peers, I don't really, I haven't succeeded.

2859
01:55:42.420 --> 01:55:46.393
I haven't really done anything, you know,

2860
01:55:47.300 --> 01:55:51.750
that led to the material success

2861
01:55:51.750 --> 01:55:54.381
that we kind of aspire towards today,

2862
01:55:54.381 --> 01:55:56.980
but I've never felt more fulfilled.

2863
01:55:56.980 --> 01:55:58.610
And I realize that the true wealth

2864
01:55:58.610 --> 01:56:00.930
is the fulfillment inside.

2865
01:56:00.930 --> 01:56:03.513
And that's, again, this is a living experiment.

2866
01:56:04.820 --> 01:56:06.580
And it's not that I'm like walking around

2867
01:56:06.580 --> 01:56:09.660
beaming all the time because I feel fulfilled inside.

2868
01:56:09.660 --> 01:56:11.810
That's not really what we're talking about.

2869
01:56:12.867 --> 01:56:16.980
It's having an inner security that wherever you are

2870
01:56:16.980 --> 01:56:18.470
is where you're supposed to be.

2871
01:56:18.470 --> 01:56:21.490
And if that means you get challenged in certain ways

2872
01:56:21.490 --> 01:56:24.540
then that challenge is there for you

2873
01:56:24.540 --> 01:56:26.477
to learn something new about yourself.

2874
01:56:26.477 --> 01:56:29.330
And that, that new thing that you learn

2875
01:56:29.330 --> 01:56:32.223
is going to add to the feeling tone of fulfillment.

2876
01:56:34.249 --> 01:56:37.830
And so that's the underlying message of this whole path,

2877
01:56:37.830 --> 01:56:39.380
is your path is not leading you

2878
01:56:39.380 --> 01:56:40.880
to more success or more comfort,

2879
01:56:40.880 --> 01:56:42.830
it's leading you to know yourself better,

2880
01:56:42.830 --> 01:56:46.240
and ultimately to feel your connection with other people.

2881
01:56:46.240 --> 01:56:47.073
And that could be

2882
01:56:47.073 --> 01:56:50.100
a very very treacherous path at some points.

2883
01:56:50.100 --> 01:56:54.620
It could be incredibly uncomfortable at other points.

2884
01:56:54.620 --> 01:56:55.920
And,

2885
01:56:55.920 --> 01:56:58.670
but the happiness that people tend to look for

2886
01:56:58.670 --> 01:57:03.450
outside in success is much more temporal

2887
01:57:03.450 --> 01:57:05.510
compared to what you can feel inside

2888
01:57:05.510 --> 01:57:07.250
while you're going through

2889
01:57:07.250 --> 01:57:10.653
all of those other moments and obstacles in life.

2890
01:57:11.630 --> 01:57:13.600
Beautifully put, man.

2891
01:57:13.600 --> 01:57:15.280
You really stuck the landing.

2892
01:57:15.280 --> 01:57:17.060
I'm like, it's not gonna get better than that.

2893
01:57:17.060 --> 01:57:18.840
Like, we should just end it right here.

2894
01:57:18.840 --> 01:57:21.640
But there is one thing I want to do before I let you go.

2895
01:57:23.190 --> 01:57:24.400
And I think this is like

2896
01:57:25.550 --> 01:57:28.490
specific to anybody who might be questioning

2897
01:57:28.490 --> 01:57:31.290
the efficacy of meditation,

2898
01:57:31.290 --> 01:57:33.847
this beautiful passage, who from the book,

2899
01:57:33.847 --> 01:57:36.500
and for those who are following along at home

2900
01:57:36.500 --> 01:57:37.563
with her own copy,

2901
01:57:38.640 --> 01:57:40.580
can find on page 80,

2902
01:57:40.580 --> 01:57:42.370
It's called So Gullible.

2903
01:57:42.370 --> 01:57:43.780
I love this, man.

2904
01:57:43.780 --> 01:57:44.613
I love this passage.

2905
01:57:44.613 --> 01:57:45.530
So can I read it?

2906
01:57:45.530 --> 01:57:46.555
Yeah.

2907
01:57:46.555 --> 01:57:47.388
I'm gonna read it.

2908
01:57:47.388 --> 01:57:48.221
Love that.

2909
01:57:48.221 --> 01:57:49.054
I'm so gullible.

2910
01:57:49.054 --> 01:57:50.960
People think meditation makes you gullible

2911
01:57:50.960 --> 01:57:53.650
but it's actually stress that makes you gullible.

2912
01:57:53.650 --> 01:57:56.310
Stress makes you crave French fries, cookies, and wine.

2913
01:57:56.310 --> 01:57:57.330
Stress makes you come up

2914
01:57:57.330 --> 01:57:59.170
with important sounding excuses

2915
01:57:59.170 --> 01:58:01.320
about why you can't exercise.

2916
01:58:01.320 --> 01:58:02.153
Stress makes you think

2917
01:58:02.153 --> 01:58:04.030
the reason you're tossing and turning at night

2918
01:58:04.030 --> 01:58:06.430
is because you don't have the right mattress.

2919
01:58:06.430 --> 01:58:09.170
Stress keeps you locked in codependent relationships

2920
01:58:09.170 --> 01:58:11.330
with emotionally unavailable partners.

2921
01:58:11.330 --> 01:58:13.530
Stress makes you say and do foolish things

2922
01:58:13.530 --> 01:58:15.570
you have to apologize for later.

2923
01:58:15.570 --> 01:58:16.730
Stress even makes you think

2924
01:58:16.730 --> 01:58:18.250
you're incapable of meditating,

2925
01:58:18.250 --> 01:58:20.250
because your mind is too busy.

2926
01:58:20.250 --> 01:58:22.260
Meanwhile, meditation makes you bold.

2927
01:58:22.260 --> 01:58:24.170
Meditation makes it really hard to put up

2928
01:58:24.170 --> 01:58:26.030
with someone else's BS.

2929
01:58:26.030 --> 01:58:27.810
Meditation makes it almost impossible

2930
01:58:27.810 --> 01:58:31.510
to remain at a dead end job or in a bad relationship.

2931
01:58:31.510 --> 01:58:33.380
Meditation makes you stand up for others

2932
01:58:33.380 --> 01:58:36.220
and follow your heart with no fallback plan.

2933
01:58:36.220 --> 01:58:38.940
Meditation allows you to be guided by your intuition

2934
01:58:38.940 --> 01:58:40.800
instead of your fear.

2935
01:58:40.800 --> 01:58:44.170
Meditation helps you accept others and let go

2936
01:58:44.170 --> 01:58:46.070
of the need to control.

2937
01:58:46.070 --> 01:58:48.640
Meditation helps you sleep like a baby,

2938
01:58:48.640 --> 01:58:51.173
even though you don't have it all figured out.

2939
01:58:52.970 --> 01:58:53.857
While I'm reading that,

2940
01:58:53.857 --> 01:58:56.110
you know where my head was the whole time?

2941
01:58:56.110 --> 01:58:57.300
Like why am I reading this?

2942
01:58:57.300 --> 01:59:00.370
I should have asked Light to read this you idiot.

2943
01:59:00.370 --> 01:59:01.203
It's his book.

2944
01:59:02.170 --> 01:59:03.380
I loved hearing it though.

2945
01:59:03.380 --> 01:59:06.000
It was such a nice experience for me to hear someone else.

2946
01:59:06.000 --> 01:59:07.710
'Cause you know, it's like you live with this stuff

2947
01:59:07.710 --> 01:59:11.120
and to hear someone else say it in their own words,

2948
01:59:11.120 --> 01:59:12.820
it's like, it's a really beautiful experience for me.

2949
01:59:12.820 --> 01:59:14.760
So thank you for gifting with that.

2950
01:59:14.760 --> 01:59:16.674
This is your Post-it note on the bridge.

2951
01:59:16.674 --> 01:59:18.160
Yeah.

2952
01:59:18.160 --> 01:59:19.570
Thank you.

2953
01:59:19.570 --> 01:59:21.000
It's great man, I love that.

2954
01:59:21.000 --> 01:59:23.930
It just breaks it down into very practical brass tacks

2955
01:59:23.930 --> 01:59:28.680
and removes all the excuses that we have.

2956
01:59:28.680 --> 01:59:32.521
Yeah, and hopefully it helps other people

2957
01:59:32.521 --> 01:59:35.140
who come across this work,

2958
01:59:35.140 --> 01:59:38.530
just look at things or consider things

2959
01:59:38.530 --> 01:59:40.350
a little differently, like meditation,

2960
01:59:40.350 --> 01:59:42.540
or whatever it is that they're questioning,

2961
01:59:42.540 --> 01:59:45.810
and find the solution within their own life experience.

2962
01:59:45.810 --> 01:59:48.823
Yeah, I think the book, you know,

2963
01:59:49.800 --> 01:59:52.050
beautifully written, all these stories, et cetera,

2964
01:59:52.050 --> 01:59:53.260
they're all prompts.

2965
01:59:53.260 --> 01:59:55.740
This is just a catalyst to get you

2966
01:59:55.740 --> 01:59:58.300
